bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535475 17592186045443 true] [17592186234275 1074 "Remember that in general, if a point $D$ has coordinates $({d}_{x},{d}_{y},{d}_{z}),$ then its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OD}=d=⟨{d}_{x},{d}_{y},{d}_{z}⟩=[\\begin{aligned}{d}_{x} \\\\ {d}_{y} \\\\ {d}_{z}\\end{aligned}]={d}_{x}\\,i+{d}_{y}\\,j+{d}_{z}\\,k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =4j-i \\\\  & =-1\\cdot i+4\\cdot j+0\\cdot k \\\\  & =⟨-1,4,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535475 17592186045443 false] [17592186234275 1074 "Remember that in general, if a point $D$ has coordinates $({d}_{x},{d}_{y},{d}_{z}),$ then its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OD}=d=⟨{d}_{x},{d}_{y},{d}_{z}⟩=\\begin{bmatrix}{d}_{x} \\\\ {d}_{y} \\\\ {d}_{z}\\end{bmatrix}={d}_{x}\\,i+{d}_{y}\\,j+{d}_{z}\\,k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =4j-i \\\\  & =-1\\cdot i+4\\cdot j+0\\cdot k \\\\  & =⟨-1,4,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535475 17592186045443 true] [17592186234276 1071 "Let $w=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$, $y=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $z=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].$ Find $2w-(3y+z).$" 13194139535475 17592186045443 false] [17592186234276 1071 "Let $w=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$, $y=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $z=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find $2w-(3y+z).$" 13194139535475 17592186045443 true] [17592186234276 1074 "To compute $2w-(3y+z),$ we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2w-(3y+z) & =2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-(3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-([\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & 